{
  "name": "Send contracts for signature with Certyneo and archive signed PDFs in Google Drive",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "certyneo-note-overview",
      "name": "Read me first",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1420,
        80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 600,
        "height": 1500,
        "content": "## Send contracts for signature with Certyneo and archive signed PDFs in Google Drive\n\n### Who's it for\n\nTeams that send contracts out for signature and want the signed file to\nend up where their records live, without anyone downloading and\nre-uploading it by hand. Certyneo is an eIDAS-compliant electronic\nsignature platform hosted in Europe.\n\n### How it works\n\nFill in the **Contract settings** node and run it: the workflow creates a\nCertyneo envelope from one of your templates and sends it to the signer.\nWhen the signer is done, Certyneo posts an event to the webhook. The\n**Crypto** node recomputes the HMAC-SHA256 of the raw body and the **If**\nnode compares it with the `X-Certyneo-Signature` header, so a forged\nevent is rejected instead of filed. Genuine `envelope.completed` events\nthen pull the sealed PDF and its audit trail from the Certyneo API and\nupload both to Google Drive.\n\n### How to set up\n\n1. In Certyneo, go to Settings then REST API and create a key with the\nenvelopes and webhooks scopes. It is shown only once.\n2. In n8n, create a **Header Auth** credential named `Authorization` whose\nvalue is `Bearer` followed by that key, and pick it on every Certyneo node.\n3. Open **Certyneo signature event**, copy its Production URL into the\n`url` field of **Register the Certyneo webhook**, and run that node once.\nThe response returns a `secret`, shown only once.\n4. Create a **Crypto** credential and paste that secret into Hmac Secret.\n5. Connect your Google Drive account on the two archive nodes.\n\n### Requirements\n\nA Certyneo account on a plan with API access, and a Google account. A\nsandbox key starting `sk_test_` runs the whole thing without emailing a\nreal signer. Only nodes shipped with n8n are used, so this works on n8n\nCloud as well as self-hosted — there is no community node to install.\n\n### How to customize\n\nThe subscription covers every Certyneo event, so to react to a refusal as\nwell, change the Filter to `envelope.declined` or swap it for a Switch.\nReplace the Google Drive nodes with S3, SharePoint or a Slack upload —\nthey consume the same `data` binary field. Swap `templateId` for\n`documentIds` to build an envelope without a saved template."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "certyneo-note-subscribe",
      "name": "Step 1 — register",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -820,
        80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 660,
        "height": 360,
        "content": "## 1. Register the webhook — run once\n\nCopy the Production URL from **Certyneo signature event** into the\n`url` field below, then run this node a single time. Keep the\n`secret` it returns: it goes into the Crypto credential."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "certyneo-note-send",
      "name": "Step 2 — send",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -820,
        440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 360,
        "content": "## 2. Send a contract\n\nEverything you need to change lives in **Contract settings**.\nCreating and sending are two calls: an envelope is born a draft,\nwhich is what lets you inspect it before it reaches the signer."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "certyneo-note-receive",
      "name": "Step 3 — verify and archive",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -820,
        800
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 1980,
        "height": 360,
        "content": "## 3. Verify, then archive\n\nThe webhook keeps the untouched request bytes in `binary.data`;\nthe Crypto node HMACs exactly those bytes, because re-serialising\nthe parsed body would only match by luck. Anything whose signature\ndoes not match stops here rather than reaching your Drive."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "certyneo-manual-subscribe",
      "name": "Run once to register the webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "position": [
        -760,
        240
      ],
      "parameters": {},
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "certyneo-subscribe",
      "name": "Register the Certyneo webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [
        -500,
        240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://certyneo.com/api/v1/webhooks",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {},
        "jsonBody": "{\n  \"url\": \"PASTE_YOUR_N8N_PRODUCTION_WEBHOOK_URL_HERE\",\n  \"events\": [\n    \"envelope.created\",\n    \"envelope.sent\",\n    \"envelope.completed\",\n    \"envelope.declined\",\n    \"envelope.voided\",\n    \"envelope.expired\",\n    \"envelope.returned_to_sender\",\n    \"envelope.resubmitted\",\n    \"recipient.signed\",\n    \"recipient.viewed\",\n    \"recipient.approved\"\n  ]\n}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "X-Certyneo-Source",
              "value": "n8n"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "certyneo-manual-send",
      "name": "Send a contract for signature",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "position": [
        -760,
        600
      ],
      "parameters": {},
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "certyneo-settings",
      "name": "Contract settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        -540,
        600
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "certyneo-cfg-template",
              "name": "templateId",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "REPLACE_WITH_A_CERTYNEO_TEMPLATE_ID"
            },
            {
              "id": "certyneo-cfg-name",
              "name": "signerName",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Jane Doe"
            },
            {
              "id": "certyneo-cfg-email",
              "name": "signerEmail",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "user@example.com"
            },
            {
              "id": "certyneo-cfg-subject",
              "name": "subject",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Contract to sign"
            },
            {
              "id": "certyneo-cfg-message",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Please review and sign."
            },
            {
              "id": "certyneo-cfg-locale",
              "name": "locale",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "en"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "certyneo-create-envelope",
      "name": "Create the envelope in Certyneo",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [
        -300,
        600
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://certyneo.com/api/v1/envelopes",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {},
        "jsonBody": "={\n  \"subject\": \"{{ $json.subject }}\",\n  \"message\": \"{{ $json.message }}\",\n  \"templateId\": \"{{ $json.templateId }}\",\n  \"recipients\": [{ \"email\": \"{{ $json.signerEmail }}\", \"name\": \"{{ $json.signerName }}\" }],\n  \"locale\": \"{{ $json.locale }}\"\n}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "X-Certyneo-Source",
              "value": "n8n"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "certyneo-send-envelope",
      "name": "Send the envelope to the signer",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [
        -60,
        600
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "=https://certyneo.com/api/v1/envelopes/{{ $json.id }}/send",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {},
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "X-Certyneo-Source",
              "value": "n8n"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "certyneo-webhook",
      "name": "Certyneo signature event",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "position": [
        -760,
        960
      ],
      "webhookId": "8f3b1c2e-5a47-4d90-91c6-2b7e0d4a6f13",
      "parameters": {
        "path": "certyneo",
        "options": {
          "rawBody": true
        },
        "httpMethod": "POST"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "certyneo-hmac",
      "name": "Compute the expected signature",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.crypto",
      "position": [
        -520,
        960
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "type": "SHA256",
        "action": "hmac",
        "encoding": "hex",
        "binaryData": true,
        "dataPropertyName": "expectedSignature",
        "binaryPropertyName": "data"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "certyneo-verify",
      "name": "Signature valid?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        -280,
        960
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "certyneo-signature-match",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.expectedSignature }}",
              "rightValue": "={{ $json.headers['x-certyneo-signature'] }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "certyneo-reject",
      "name": "Reject the forged event",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stopAndError",
      "position": [
        -40,
        1160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "errorMessage": "Rejected a Certyneo event whose X-Certyneo-Signature did not match. Check that the Crypto credential holds the secret returned when the webhook was registered."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "certyneo-filter",
      "name": "Keep completed envelopes only",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.filter",
      "position": [
        -40,
        940
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "certyneo-event-completed",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.body.event }}",
              "rightValue": "envelope.completed"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
